# Arena — the ranked answer

**The best three ideas per area, and why they beat each other.**

This file is the deliverable. It is rewritten in place every pass and is
meant to be short enough to reason over. If it grows, a pass appended
instead of replacing — that is a bug, and `scripts/arena_invariants.py`
check C11 fails when it happens.

All supporting evidence — every tranche note, qualification, contradiction,
measurement and citation — lives in **`ARENA-EVIDENCE.md`**, which is
append-only and never pruned. Nothing is deleted: every line of the
pre-split file is in exactly one of the two files.

