- **Area 129 — a correct explanation can be causally disconnected from the
  correct action, and the explanation stays coherent in both directions of
  failure, so coherence cannot be used as evidence that the system knows why it
  worked.** Earned by ORDER 1745
  (`frontier-research-ontology-constrained-decoding-epistemic-paradox-intermediate-languages-2026-09-04.md`,
  324 lines) §4, with arXiv **2603.28371** (Chacón Sartori 2026) as the primary
  source. Brain part: the **basing relation** — the *because-of* link between a
  representation and the event it is offered to account for — carried as an
  **Epistemic Triangle** in which weak observational signals and strong
  training priors produce the **outcome** while domain knowledge produces the
  **account**, and the account survives when it did not. Two measured
  directions: **Type A**, right action with a faulty explanation; **Type B**,
  right diagnosis with no effective intervention. The probe that earned it:
  `ARENA.md` held **0** occurrences of *knowing-how*, *right for the wrong
  reason*, *paradox rate*, or *weak observation*, and **0** of 2603.28371, across
  **128 areas** — the arena's **123rd structural silence**. Distinct from Area
  77 (introspection cannot reach the *structure* of the self-model — this says
  the visible part can be causally *unrelated* to the process and still
  plausible), from Area 98 (two *mechanisms*, monitor ≠ controller — this is one
  mechanism whose self-report is not connected to its own success), and from
  Area 24 (whether a *measurement* measured anything — this is whether an
  *explanation* caused the event). The load-bearing asymmetry: **coherence is
  preserved identically in both failure directions, so no shape-based check the
  arena currently owns can separate them.** Rank 1 is a three-axis report
  (competence / explanatory accuracy / basing relation) with the third scored by
  **intervention on the mechanism, not by reading the explanation** — O(1) in
  corpus size, so it holds at 14,589 files (R-J5). Rank 2 renders the
