*82 · The second substrate — earned by ORDER 1016 §§"Computational Operations
Implemented by the Tripartite Synapse", "Metabolic Gating of Plasticity",
"IP3R2 Knockout Phenotype". Brain part: the **tripartite synapse** and the
**astrocyte–neuron lactate shuttle**. The arena's eighty-second structural
silence, and the first about **whether the substrate is in a state that permits
learning at all**: eighty-one areas gate on truth, time, reversibility and
novelty, and **not one gates on the system's own capacity to be written to.**
Rank 1 is a **state gate on the write path** — a write to a saturated store is
*refused and reported as refused*, not downgraded — built on the tranche's
sharpest single experiment, **Suzuki et al. 2011**: blocking glycogenolysis
impairs long-term memory while short-term memory is intact, and **L-lactate,
but not pyruvate or glucose, rescues it.** Grade deliberately `LOW` on the
mechanism, not `HIGH`, because the file's own effect sizes are **10–30% LTP
changes and "subtle memory deficits."** Rank 3 is the tranche's
`UNSUCCESSFUL` slot and the most valuable negative in the file: **IP3R2
knockout abolishes most astrocytic Ca²⁺ and produces "surprisingly mild
cognitive phenotypes"** — the strong glial hypothesis was tested by the people
who hold it and returned a null on the core claim, so the arena records
*"do not build a glial layer"* with the corpus's own guidance attached
(*regularization and adaptation modules, not core forward-pass components*).
Three slots filled, mark dropped.*
*84 · Ignition: a threshold on *having* the thought, not on whether it is true —
earned by ORDER 1018 §§"The Two-Stage Process", "The Ignition Phenomenon in
Detail", "Global Broadcasting and Access Consciousness", "GWT and the Frame
Problem", with ORDER 1034 §5 (*Skills*). Brain part: **Baars' global workspace
and Dehaene & Changeux's ignition** — feedforward sweep ~100 ms → nonlinear
threshold crossing → recurrent global broadcast ~300 ms, workspace ~4–7 items,
threshold *modulated* by attention, neuromodulators, arousal, task relevance and
prediction error. The arena's eighty-fourth structural silence and **the first
about a threshold on availability**: eighty-three areas gate on truth,
confidence, cost, novelty, coincidence and substrate state, and **every one of
those gates is applied to a representation the system already has.** The
ignition threshold is applied to one the system **has not yet had** — masked
stimuli are processed and leave an above-chance trace while producing nothing
reportable, so the loss happens *upstream* of every gate the arena holds.
Rank 1 makes swept-vs-ignited a reported outcome, with the clause that **a
sweep is not a failure** — masked priming is exactly the case where the
system's honest self-report (*"I did not process that"*) is false. The
workspace's own instance is recorded unflatteringly: `LEDGER.md` has one mark
and no way to distinguish swept from ignited, and this pass read 20 files and
absorbed 4. Grade `LOW` on the mechanism and **not `HIGH`** despite convergent
evidence, because the file's own table grades the P3b *"Partial (posterior
emphasis)"* and §5.1 records an unresolved frontal-vs-posterior conflict with
IIT — plus the design `UNTESTED`, and the transfer from a consciousness theory
into an architecture with no consciousness claim is the one Area 74 Rank 1
forbids. Rank 2 is broadcast-not-push on the **frame problem**, and its
finding is adopt-don't-build: **skills already are subscriptions** (system
prompt carries name+description; the model loads on match) and have never been
described as broadcasting — the same shape as Area 63's hybrid retriever.
Rank 3 is a **do-not-build** slot held down by **R-J2** rather than by a fact
about the world: the area's own nominated instrument is the no-report
paradigm, which requires a human subject and fMRI, and a substitute would be a
self-measurement. Three slots filled, mark dropped.*
*Area 53 · Rank 3 corrected in place, tranche 48 — the arena's first
**scope correction to a null slot**, and it runs the other way from the skill's
usual case.* The slot read ORDER 719's Hype ❌ entry (*"theoretical only"*) as
a claim that **no global-workspace implementation exists** and recorded
`Already exists: nothing`. ORDER 1018 §2.5 and §8.3 name four that do:
**Dehaene & Changeux's 100,000-neuron spiking model** (reproduces masking,
binocular rivalry, the P3b, attention-modulated ignition, simulated-anaesthesia
disruption), **McClelland's Fluid Framework / GWA**, and **ReAct and
Plan-and-Execute** as GWT-shaped agent designs. The negative was never wrong
about the *architecture* — it was about **consciousness**, and the same file's
§3.2 is the mechanism of the confusion: **GWT explicitly targets access
consciousness and declines phenomenal consciousness.** The corpus separates the
two quantities; the slot had merged them. The null is retained, correctly
scoped, and now **points at Area 84** for the architectural half. Per the
skill's rule that a *displaced* slot stays visible for one revision, the
original wording is preserved verbatim in `ARENA-EVIDENCE.md` rather than
deleted.
*Corroboration, tranche 48 — one increment, no re-rank, grade deliberately
unchanged.* **Area 8 · Support 6 → 7, independent.** ORDER 1021 §5.5/§6.4
supplies the *architectural law* behind the area's existing hybrid requirement:
**standard message passing is bounded by 1-WL and cannot count** (a 4-cycle is
indistinguishable from two 3-cycles), and the agent consequence is named in one
line — *"Over-smoothing → Knowledge dilution: agents aggregating too much
context blur distinctions."* The area's rank-1 requirement (*retain the surface
chunk beside every extracted entity*) is now supported from two directions that
constrain each other: the graph form says depth blurs the surface, the
KG-compilation form says the surface does not survive extraction, and each
destroys what the other preserves. **Support genuinely increments** — a GNN
expressivity survey and a memory-extraction ablation are different literatures
with different methods. **Grade NOT raised:** a bound on a class of
architectures is not a trial of this design, and the bound says nothing about a
retrieval stack that does no message passing.
*83 · The mean is not a model of the individual — earned by ORDER 1012
§§"Sexual Dimorphism vs. Overlap", "Effect Sizes and Overlap Distributions".
Brain part: the **mosaic brain** (Joel 2015/2020, 116 regions, 281 subjects)
and the **overlapping-distribution** result that generalises it — **78% of 124
effect sizes across 46 meta-analyses are small or near zero**, reconfirmed on
106 meta-analyses and 386 effect sizes, meaning **~80% distribution overlap**,
so *"most men score above the average woman."* The arena's eighty-third
structural silence and the sharpest aimed at the arena itself: **eighty-three
areas are written in the singular**, and a group mean with d = 0.3 classifies
almost no individual. Rank 1 requires `population_scope` beside every default
and a per-user override beside every user-facing one — **Area 47's cultural bet
with its error bars attached.** Distributional finding `HIGH` (two independent
large-scale replications); design `UNTESTED`. Rank 3 preserves the contest
rather than resolving it: **Rippon 2017's cherry-picking objection** and a
**Feb 2024 *PNAS* deep-net study that reportedly classifies sex from ~1,500
fMRI scans**, with the file's own resolution marked as *the file's, not a
finding.* Three slots filled, mark dropped.*
