*96 · The substrate is a budget, and exhaustion has an order — earned by ORDER
1231 (`Metabolic-Cognition/Brain-Energy-Budget-Ketone-Fasting.md`, 291 lines).
Brain part: the **metabolic-demand hierarchy of the CNS** and its behavioural
shadow. The arena's ninety-sixth structural silence, and the first about **what
the system gives up rather than what it refuses**: ninety-five areas hold gates —
on truth (33), time (81), reversibility (25), novelty (27), substrate state
(82) — **and a gate says no while never saying what goes instead.** Area 82 asked
whether the substrate permits a write; nothing asked which function dies first
when the budget runs short. The corpus's answer is an *order* and not a
magnitude: complex executive function fails first, attention and working memory
next, simple motor function preserved longest — **mirroring per-gram metabolic
rate**, so vulnerability is a property of energy intensity, not of importance.
Rank 1 makes that order a declared field with **deferral reported as
deferral**; the clause is the whole design, because a system that silently drops
its most expensive function and returns a cheap answer has produced a confident
wrong answer — the failure this arena names in nine areas and, until this pass,
in this one. Human mechanism `LOW` and deliberately not `HIGH`; the file's own
§"Individual Differences" records the order is **not uniform** across diabetes,
aging, GLUT1/3 variation and prior hypoglycaemic episodes, so a single global
order is a first approximation the corpus already qualifies, and the
qualification is carried in the slot rather than dropped for tidiness. Rank 2 is
the substrate as a **latent variable** the controller can read and cannot
introspect honestly — the file asks as an open question whether metabolic
self-monitoring is accessible to cognitive control, and a slot built on an open
question is held at `UNTESTED` rather than promoted because the arena wants an
answer. Rank 3 is **`UNSUCCESSFUL` and is the tranche's most valuable negative**:
the fasting→BDNF→consolidation-window analogy is the tranche's most attractive
and its weakest, and the corpus records the verdict itself — **Martin et al.
(2006) found no significant cognitive differences in a large randomised trial** —
so the offline window this workspace already runs must be kept on operational
grounds and **may not be cited as physiological support**. Three slots filled,
mark dropped.*
*97 · The architecture of the memory system is itself the plastic variable —
earned by ORDER 1230 (`round85-2026-09-12.md` §1, **MemEvolve**, arXiv 2512.18746,
ICML 2026). **The brain-part naming here is the arena's mapping, not the file's
claim** — the file supplies the mechanism and the measurement and names no
anatomy, and the arena says so rather than borrowing a citation it did not earn.
The arena's ninety-seventh structural silence, and the first one level above
Area 66: metaplasticity makes the **learning rate** a function of recent
activity; this makes the **architecture** one. Rank 1 is bilevel evolution over
a declared **Encode/Store/Retrieve/Manage** design space, with the outer loop
selecting on a **tournament over held-out tasks** — measured at **+17.06%** over
SmolAgent and Flash-Searcher with **2.0–9.09%** transfer to unseen backbones,
which is `LOW` and not `HIGH` because the file's own `UNCERTAINTIES` block says
broader generalisation is untested and its `CONFLICTS` block concedes
hand-designed systems have **interpretability and control advantages that were
not measured** — the trade this arena cares about most, since a self-evolving
schema is unauditable by construction while `ARENA.md` is auditable precisely
because its schema is fixed. Rank 1 is therefore also flagged **against the
workspace's own checkers**, which assume a fixed ledger schema and slot format.
Rank 2 reads the three evolved architectures (Riva, Cerebra, Lightweight) as
**descriptive findings about the design space**, which survives the objection
rank 1 cannot: if the outer loop cannot be audited, its output can still be read.
Rank 3 is the slot the tranche actually needed — **the arena's own method is a
self-reinforcing loop and it has no holdout**, which Area 62 Rank 3 recorded as
a silent constraint and MemEvolve supplies the only known mechanism for
detecting. `UNTESTED`, and per R-J2 **this is not a proposal to measure the
arena**: it is the observation that a saturated method and a working method
produce identical ledgers, identical arena files and identical PASS verdicts.
Three slots filled, mark dropped.*
*Corroborations, tranche 56 — **one increment, one reach, no re-rank, no grade
change:*
- **Area 12 · Support 6 → 7, independent.** ORDER 1229 (`round84-2026-09-11.md`
  §1, **Procedural Graphs**, arXiv 2609.09153, Google Research) gives "what-to-do"
  the same explicit treatment "what-is" has long had, and earns the increment on
  two counts. (1) The **self-evolution loop is gated and keeps its rejections**:
  diagnostic rollout → feedback-driven mutation → **validation gate**
  (`val(G_cand) ≥ val(G_retained)`) → **rejection memory** where rejected
  candidates are *retained as negative constraints* — the first source in this
  arena's history that makes keeping the rejected candidate part of the design
  rather than an audit convention, and it is this workspace's own `SKILL.md`
  rule arriving as published engineering. (2) A **static expert PG matches or
  surpasses hand-designed graphs and a self-evolved one matches or exceeds the
  expert PG**, which is a real narrowing of the area's `curated >
  self-generated` reading rather than a restatement of it. Grade held at `LOW`:
  this is a benchmark of a procedure store, not a trial of the area's
  proceduralization mechanism. **Two requirements it earns, both cutting against
  the existing slots:** the validation gate must read a **held-out** score,
  because a candidate adopted by the model that also judged it is exactly the
  self-graded shape **Area 95** shows compounding — and the **soft-constraint**
  design (edge attributes *bias* without *dictating*) is the first source here
  that separates a procedure which **guides** from one which **compells**, the
  distinction Areas 4 and 12 both need and neither states.
- **Area 8 · Support unchanged, reach confirmed.** ORDER 1230 §5 restates the
  **Hallucination Snowball** (arXiv 2608.14588), which ORDER 1170 already
  supplies, so per the one-source rule it adds **reach, not replication**. What
  it adds is the **quantitative chain** the arena's version lacked: per-boundary
  escape probabilities **24.6% / 48.3% / 89.3%** over **346 injected
  hallucinations**, GPT-4o detection **72.0% → 50.9%**, **23.7% surviving
  entirely**, and the law stated as a generality — **"when you verify matters
  more than whether you verify"**, boundary gates cutting survival **58.4% →
  16.2%** against **2.3 pp** for end-of-pipeline checking. It also supplies a
  **ceiling the arena did not hold**: the strongest model tested projects only
  **60–65%** Stage-4 detection, so the snowball is **not** a detector-quality
  problem and a better detector does not close it. Recorded limitation: the
  model **assumes a linear pipeline**, which is the shape of every multi-agent
  design in this arena.
