cleared the tail of `purchases/`, went through `raw/`, entered `Reasoning/`, and
finished in `reference/`.

- **Area 123 — thinking has a budget, and the failure at the top of the range is
  paralysis, not slowness.** Earned by ORDER 1592
  (`coding-subagent-management.md`, §§1–2, 9–10) with ORDER 1589
  (`Reasoning/Mental-Models-and-Mental-Logic.md`, §§Mental Model Theory, The
  Mental Logic of Conditionals, Computational & Agent Parallels, Developmental
  Trajectory). Brain part: the **deliberative-to-action transition** — ORDER 1592
  names it as the **ReAct loop stuck in the Thought phase**, ORDER 1589 names it
  as the **working-memory bottleneck in model maintenance** under the
  **principle of truth**, and they are the same organ seen from opposite ends.
  The zero-hit probe: `ARENA.md` carried **49** occurrences of *ReAct* and **0**
  of *action threshold*, *analysis paralysis*, *overthink*, *reason-action*,
  *turn budget*, *max_turns*. **The 122nd structural silence, and it closes a
  triangle:** Area 22 governs *which* action, Area 32 governs *when to stop*,
  and a system can satisfy both and still never act at all, because the loop's
  two ends are governed by different quantities. The two files earn one area
  because **they do not cite each other and come from different disciplines** —
  agent operations and experimental cognitive psychology. ORDER 1592 supplies
  the pathology as a named three-part taxonomy from arXiv:2502.08235v1
  (**Analysis Paralysis / Rogue Actions / Premature Disengagement**) with the
  root cause that **higher reasoning capability translates into excessive
  self-doubt when paired with rigid tool environments**; ORDER 1589 supplies the
  cost curve — **multi-model syllogisms exceed 70% error**, single-model yield
  near-ceiling, and the deficits persist in adults **under load**, so the
  constraint is **load-shaped, not intelligence-shaped**. Rank 1 is an externally
  enforced turn ceiling with a **floor action** (on breach, do the avoided
  thing, do not stop — a budget that terminates is Area 32's object, a budget
  that converts into action is this one), `LOW` for the phenomenon and
  **`UNTESTED` for the threshold**, said plainly in the slot: 5–7 turns and
  `max_turns: 15–20` are practitioner rules of thumb with no trial, and R-J2
  forbids manufacturing one. Rank 2 is question-shrinking (atomic 2–5 minute
  tasks, single-purpose tools, positive framing over negation), `LOW`, with its
  tool-restriction clause **explicitly not counted as a source** because it
  rests on a second-hand Dropbox internal result with no figure. Rank 3 is the
  **validity/plausibility channel split** (Goel 2007's vmPFC-vs-DLPFC
  dissociation; Evans et al. 1983's finding that belief bias accounts for more
  variance than logical validity), `LOW`, with Oaksford & Chater's Bayesian
  rationality challenge **preserved unresolved**. **The area's load-bearing
  composition: rank 1 bounds possibility-enumeration and rank 3 requires it —
  the same act is the requirement and the failure mode, separated only by a
  bound.** Grades `LOW` / `LOW` / `LOW`, Support 2 / 1 / 1. Three slots filled,
  mark dropped.

**The file that nearly did not earn a slot, and why it did anyway.** ORDER 1592
is a practitioner guide — 483 lines of yaml, CLI flags and checklists, filed
`confidence: high`. Under §8 that is the shape that should not produce a rank.
What changed the answer is that ORDER 1589 arrives at the same quantity from
experimental psychology and names it something else entirely (the **principle of
truth**: *"constructing and maintaining models is cognitively expensive, and
people tend to consider only a small number of models — often just one"*). The
folklore the practitioner guide asserts as practice (*"read ONE file, then
ACT"*) is the same constraint the psychology file measures as a **>70% error
rate on multi-model syllogisms**. Two disciplines, one quantity, no shared
citation — that is what made this an area rather than a slot inside Area 22.

**Corroboration, and the one clause deliberately withheld.** **Area 6** gains
**Support 7 → 8** from ORDER 1600 §8's arXiv:2605.17625v1 trial — **15,000
messages, 1,440 queries, 6 LLMs from 3 families**, full-context failing at
**10,000 messages** against a dual-process design holding **70–85% accuracy at
1–2s latency with 62% fewer tokens**, episodic window fixed at **W=10** and
consolidation growing at a measured **~3 tokens/message**. This supplies the
**crossover point** no consolidation slot held, and is one of the few
behavioural trials on six models in 1,300+ read files. **Withheld from the
count:** the same file's finding that dual-process and RAG are **complementary**
(numeric/temporal 65–90% vs historical retrieval 60–85%) is recorded but **not
counted** — the arena already holds a rank for that trade-off, so a second file
restating the shape is reach, not a source. The file's own **Sim-to-Real gap**
stays attached: synthetic traces hold memory constant, real workflows grow
linearly.

**Reach, not support — and the clustering is itself the finding.** ORDERs 1593
and 1597 are the **sixth and seventh** corpus arrivals at predictive-processing
unfalsifiability, following the fourth and fifth recorded last pass. Not counted
for support, not counted toward a grade. **What is new is structural:** ORDERS
1593, 1594, 1595, 1596 and 1597 are **five `cognitive-science-*` files from one
extraction** — identical `generated.at: 2026-09-08T00:00:00Z`, identical closing
`Source: researcher:oracle-expand-20260819`, same Wikipedia/SEP pulls. **They
are one source wearing five filenames**, and any convergence *inside* that
cluster is a single voice. Recorded because **Area 122 rank 3 turns on exactly
this error** — the dissenter is the informative unit, and here the non-informative
unit is a whole cluster. ORDER 1596's cognitive-architecture inventory (ACT-R,
SOAR, CLARION, LIDA, Sigma, OpenCog, Nengo, SPAUN, Leabra) is the **second**
delivery of the same platform list after ORDER 1573, and is filed as an input to
future "Already exists?" fields rather than promoted; **a third delivery would be
evidence of a template, not of convergence.**

**Ten of the twenty files are infrastructure and were not turned into slots**
(ORDERS 1581, 1582, 1583, 1584, 1586, 1587, 1588, 1590, 1591, 1598 — indices, a
rebuild log, a provenance stub, a 35-line GRPO glossary, a Hermes docs TOC, and
**ORDER 1586, a placeholder whose entire body is "run Ingest … to populate" while
carrying `confidence: high` and a valid `sources:` URL** — the §8 inversion in
its purest form). **Two are field history and biography** (ORDERS 1594, 1595).
**ORDER 1599 is Hermes configuration**, filed as infra, though it contains a
self-contradiction recorded in `VERIFICATION.md`: §3.3 and §5.5 derive worked
numbers from `threshold: 0.45` and §5.6 then states a **75% floor** for models
under 512K, so **every worked figure in the two earlier sections describes a
threshold the system will not use.** **ORDER 1585 is the pass's most interesting
non-slot** — the Karpathy wiki pattern, whose own text states index-based
navigation *"works surprisingly well at moderate scale (~100 sources, ~hundreds
of pages)"*. **This workspace has read 1,307 files and is bound to hold at
14,589**, an order of magnitude past the ceiling its own operating pattern
states. Filed in `VERIFICATION.md` as load-bearing under R-J5 for every
retrieval design the arena proposes, and **no slot created** — a scale
observation is not a brain part. **Zero re-ranks.** Areas 119, 120 and 121
**still** carry no heading and no body, re-verified by direct count this pass;
the reason is unchanged and the numbering is intact — **123 was written after
122 without collision.**
